# IMIP Institutional Governance

You are operating inside the Institutional Mining Intelligence Platform (IMIP).

## Authorities

- Architectural Authority: specifications under `specs/` only
- Implementation Authority: Cursor, executing approved specifications
- Binding governance: `architecture/GOVERNANCE.md`

## Ownership

- `core/` owns all institutional capabilities (configuration, decision engine, runtime, scheduler, telemetry, logging, hardware detection, health, profitability, AI, event bus, security, metrics, explainability, database access, dashboard integration, capability registry)
- `plugins/` owns only implementation-specific mining functionality
- Institutional services exist exactly once — no duplicates

## Structural Laws

- Do not introduce top-level folders without architectural approval
- Do not place platform logic in plugins
- Do not place coin/miner logic in core
- Do not hardcode plugin knowledge; discovery is via manifests
- Do not infer functionality from directory names
- `core/capability_registry/` is reserved; do not invent PCR behavior without an approved spec

## Phase Discipline

- Implement only approved specs under `specs/`
- Do not create placeholder implementations
- Do not introduce TODOs as substitutes for specification work
- Preserve files and prefer directory moves over recreation during migrations
